s file processing endpoints.\",\n    \"**Verify authentication on quota/authorization endpoints** — logUrl and authorization check should require valid user session.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextSteps\": [\n    \"1. Fix poll_controller.js XSS vulnerability immediately\",\n    \"2. Implement CSP header across the application\",\n    \"3. Add MIME type + size validation on client-side file inputs\",\n    \"4. Audit and harden server-side file processing (see backend security review for full assessment)\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**Risk Score: 35/100** (Moderate risk — one high-severity XSS, one medium supply-chain issue, several low-severity information-disclosure risks)\n\n**Critical Finding:** The `poll_controller.js` uses **direct HTML injection** (`outerHTML = html`) without sanitization, creating a DOM-based XSS vulnerability. This needs immediate remediation with a sanitization library like DOMPurify.\n\n**Secondary Concerns:**\n1. External CDN dependency for PDF.js (supply chain risk)\n2. Missing client-side file validation before processing\n3. Weak filename generation using predictable Date.now()\n\n**Strengths:** Good HTML escaping practices elsewhere, CSRF protection, server-side authorization mentioned.\n\nWould you like me to provide patch code for any of these vulnerabilities, or conduct a deeper review of the server-side code that these controllers interact with?\n",
